A||N||2||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||Small Back fire when pulling from a stop?||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||05-24-2000||01:30 AM||||<BR>I just started getting a small back fire when I pull away from a stop, a couple of days ago.  It doesn't happen all of the time, just sometimes. I have no codes poping up.  So, what could be causing it?<BR>Thanks for your help.<BR>Jeff||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||09:44 AM||||My '84 SE used to backfire before we straightened out the timing.<P>Hope this helps!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-24-2000||09:46 AM||||check for ignition problems and distributor base timing.<P>run a decent brand of injector cleaner thru it.<P>check for vacuum leaks might be a small one some place.<P>check the vacuum line to the MAP sensor very carefully. check the MAP electrical connector. make sure the MAP line is connected to the right fitting on the engine. replace the MAP. MAP is used by the ECM to calculate "vacuum advance" for the timing. if it's bad or the vacuum line is leaking, too long, or blocked, then it can do this kind of thing. <P>The MAP vacuum line should be kept short as posible when it's replaced.||||reg||1
